) Stromal counts of FOXP3-positive cells in MSS and MSI-H colorectal cancers. (<bold>C</bold>) The ratio of epithelial-to-stromal FOXP3-positive cell counts in MSS and MSI-H colorectal cancers. <italic>Y</italic> axis was truncated at 0.4, &#x000a7; represents one extreme value at 0.7. Open circles represent outliers (above 1.5 interquartile ranges), <sup>&#x0002a;</sup> represent extreme values (above 3 interquartile ranges).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="eps" xlink:href="6604756f2"/></fig><fig id="fig3"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Representative immunofluorescence stainings. Double stainings for CD8 (Alexa Fluor 488, green) and FOXP3 (Alexa Fluor 594, red) in the left panel and centre panel, respectively. Double staining for CD3 (Alexa Fluor 488, green) and FOXP3 (Alexa Fluor 594, red) in the right panel.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="eps" xlink:href="6604756f3"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Characteristics of CRC patients</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="char" char="("/><col align="char" char="("/><col align="left"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" char="(" charoff="50"><bold>MSA status</bold><hr/></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th></tr><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Total</bold></th><th align="char" valign="top" char="(" charoff="50"><bold>MSI-H</bold></th><th align="char" valign="top" char="(" charoff="50"><bold>MSS</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold><italic>P</italic>-value<sup>a</sup></bold></t